                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d51d27a6-49e3-4f31-8714-1dfb646c64be",
                                                "sense_id": "5a34f8fc-63db-39cb-a8aa-322cdeab6829",
                                                "text": "Not long since O’Connell beat the sceptic geologists of the British Association of nonsense and “science” all to nothing by a discovery of fossil Whigs—very extraordinary and ferocious creatures they must have been in their day, which, of course, was far anterior to the creation of the world, according to the Mosaic account, which the bone-grubbing “philosophers” of the chalk formations have so properly exploded."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb9e1d94-a881-46e6-9018-37a0fdd9bda9",
                                                "sense_id": "5a34f8fc-63db-39cb-a8aa-322cdeab6829",
                                                "text": "The black race, much inferior to the Arab in intellectual power and in steadiness of will, are at the same time free from the sceptic distrustfulness and deep jealousy so common among their white fellow-citizens."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5fc5b24-a1c4-4a80-a775-67a079c427b7",
                                                "sense_id": "5a34f8fc-63db-39cb-a8aa-322cdeab6829",
                                                "text": "As I said, my experience was: I travelled to Russia as a sceptic person and I returned as a European."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "370816b4-fae6-44e8-afe3-f92fe2d6e954",
                        "source_entry_id": "04c4edf7-3beb-301a-a9b5-68ede90e2f23",
                        "target_lang_word": "sceptical",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sceptical",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d39149a2-9191-3b09-a2d4-22b2591f37b5",
                                        "entry_id": "9934267b-8e6c-3ef7-bd0f-6977be3db581",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Commonwealth standard spelling of skeptical."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42b79e3c-3245-47d7-946f-aedfc8a57517",
                                                "sense_id": "d39149a2-9191-3b09-a2d4-22b2591f37b5",
                                                "text": "But regardless of what they made of phrenology, those who saw craniometry as a means of measuring the relative weight of intelligence and emotion in psychological makeup were generally sceptical as to whether, as Blumenbach and Camper believed, humanity had branched from one ancestral pair into varietal types as a result of colonising different continents."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e77be4bc-1005-4810-b6f7-22375b25375d",
                                                "sense_id": "d39149a2-9191-3b09-a2d4-22b2591f37b5",
                                                "text": "And according to Hughes, HM Treasury is still sceptical about rail electrification. \"It's not because they don't see electrification as a good thing, but I think when you look at it from the UK-wide perspective, if you have £x billion to spend on decarbonisation, you don't necessarily start with rail. Rail's not where you get the biggest bang for the buck in terms of decarbonisation.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d83f1c1a-e561-45f5-b0fe-aa5f9ab4cdcc",
                        "source_entry_id": "04c4edf7-3beb-301a-a9b5-68ede90e2f23",
                        "target_lang_word": "skeptisch",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "skeptisch",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "801a806a-0257-3bb0-9fb2-3bda1e992811",
                                        "entry_id": "42232f26-7b9a-3b42-87a8-131a11cbbfcc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "zum Zweifel geneigt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
